// Extended grapheme cluster segmentation: UAX #29 (Unicode 17.0.0) over UTF-8
// views, https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr29/ section 3.1.1. A cluster is what
// a reader sees as one character: a base with its combining marks, a Hangul
// syllable spelled as jamo, an emoji ZWJ sequence, a flag pair, an Indic
// conjunct. The rules GB1 to GB13 and GB999 are implemented as a state machine
// over the Grapheme_Cluster_Break class of each scalar plus two auxiliary
// properties (Extended_Pictographic for GB11, Indic_Conjunct_Break for GB9c),
// so a decision costs one table lookup and a bounded state; nothing allocates
// and nothing recurses. `spec/lean/Oak/GraphemeBreak.lean` states the rules
// and this machine and proves them equivalent.
//
// Ill-formed UTF-8: an undecodable byte is its own cluster (a boundary before
// and after it), so segmentation is total over any byte view and every offset
// it returns lands on a scalar boundary of the well-formed stretches.
